gomad: stop expanding no-op select-poll decisions after a soundness check
- The explorer leaves a select-poll decision unexpanded when its select
  polled two cases and recorded a readiness of one of the seven fixture
  shapes with fewer than two ready cases; anything else, including an
  unknown readiness, stays expanded. The skipped alternatives are counted
  in omitted_by_select_readiness beside the depth and execution bounds and
  make no stop reason.
- The rule is the v3 controller identity, so a journal written under v2 is
  refused on resume; the retained pre-start-ordinal journal is re-encoded
  under v3 with its decisions unchanged and its pins updated.
- The select-readiness fixture explores every shape to exhaustion in full
  and reduced and records whether the two agree; a listed shape that does
  not fails the fixture. All seven listed shapes agree (reduced
  96/32/32/96/32/32/96 executions against full 196/68/68/196/68/68/200).
- Signal suite seed 11 on build 2008ea81: 57,696 decisions, of which the
  explorer now expands 42,918; trace bytes unchanged at 8,262,720. No-op
  decisions stay in the Choice Trace; the decision and its numbers are in
  the spec's Decision Context and under select-reduction/.

